The evaluator's verdict was precise: deliverables 1, 2 and 4 had landed and verified live; deliverable 3 — the dated census in CLAUDE.md — was skipped a third time, with all three prior commits touching only scripts/check_assertion_weakening.py.

Step 0 re-measured rather than trusted the receipt, and it confirmed the evaluator on all four points: the five CONVENTION_* constants now have two readers (render_conventions_limit() and the conv_fixtures table), LIMITS item 5 renders from WRITTEN_CONVENTIONS, the source says the finding is UNFILED and #914 is the harness's auto-filed receipt, and --test exits 0. So the only remaining work was the CLAUDE.md paragraph.

## The census, measured rather than cited

Re-running was not too slow, so I did not take the task's escape hatch for the live half:

• **Window depth read from the tool: `git rev-list --count HEAD` → 60 commits, shallow=true**, so HEAD~40 spans ~one day — LIMITS item 4 demonstrating itself.
• **Net scan HEAD~40..HEAD*: 40 commits · 27 `.rs` hunks · 6 test-file hunks — WEAKENED 0 · STRENGTHENED 6 · UNKNOWN 0 · MOVED 0.
• **Per-commit, same window (stricter): 40 · 32 · 7 — WEAKENED 0 · STRENGTHENED 6 · UNKNOWN 1** · MOVED 0, the UNKNOWN being aa29fe9d src/help.rs, counted and reported.

The four counts are never summed, and the two modes are reported separately rather than pooled — they cover different hunk populations (27 vs 32).

Zero `WEAKENED` live means there was nothing to attribute today, so the per-convention column is the Day-196 reading, labelled as the dated reading it was rather than presented as current. That is the one place I used the escape hatch, and I said so in the paragraph instead of letting a stale number read as fresh.

## The finding that outranks the counts

The table records that 4 of 5 predictions held and 1 was falsified, and that register-paid-to-empty → WEAKENED is not a false positive: paying a register to empty deletes the anti-vacuous guard, which is a real assert! removed with none added back. It stays pinned WEAKENED on purpose — downgrading it would manufacture a clean bill over a genuine coverage reduction. I also recorded the second falsification the constants themselves carry: whole-file-test-rename is handled by two mechanisms (--diff-filter=d exclusion in per-commit mode, MOVED in the net scan), and the Day-196 prediction named only the second.

